 ('ENT_ISR_JOB','PER_ISR_IRON_AGE','A blameless man of Uz whose endurance of catastrophic suffering frames the book''s debate on divine justice.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_EZRA','PER_ISR_EXILIC','Priest and scribe who led returning exiles and re-established the Torah in restored Jerusalem.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_NEHEMIAH','PER_ISR_EXILIC','Cupbearer to the Persian king who became governor and rebuilt the walls of Jerusalem and reformed the community.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_LATTER_PROPHETS','PER_ISR_IRON_AGE','The prophetic canon division comprising the three Major Prophets and the Book of the Twelve, spanning the Assyrian, Babylonian, and Persian periods.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_TWELVE_PROPHETS','PER_ISR_IRON_AGE','A single scroll in the Hebrew canon gathering twelve shorter prophetic books from the 8th century BCE to the post-exilic restoration.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_ISAIAH','PER_ISR_IRON_AGE','An 8th-century BCE Judahite prophet whose oracles warn of judgment yet promise a remnant, a Davidic messiah, and a restored Zion.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_JEREMIAH','PER_ISR_EXILIC','A late 7th- to early 6th-century BCE prophet who foretold Jerusalem''s fall to Babylon and proclaimed a coming new covenant written on the heart.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_EZEKIEL','PER_ISR_EXILIC','A 6th-century BCE priest-prophet among the Babylonian exiles whose visions of the chariot, dry bones, and a restored temple promise renewal.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_DANIEL_PROPHET','PER_ISR_EXILIC','A Judahite exile at the Babylonian and Persian courts whose faithfulness and apocalyptic visions affirm God''s rule over the kingdoms of the world.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_HOSEA','PER_ISR_IRON_AGE','An 8th-century BCE prophet to the northern kingdom whose troubled marriage dramatizes Israel''s faithlessness and God''s enduring covenant love.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_JOEL','PER_ISR_IRON_AGE','A prophet of Judah who reads a devastating locust plague as a sign of the coming Day of the Lord and promises an outpouring of God''s Spirit.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_AMOS','PER_ISR_IRON_AGE','A mid-8th-century BCE Judahite shepherd who prophesied against the northern kingdom, condemning injustice and empty worship.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_OBADIAH','PER_ISR_EXILIC','Author of the shortest book of the Hebrew Bible, an oracle of judgment against Edom for its betrayal of Judah.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_JONAH','PER_ISR_IRON_AGE','A reluctant prophet, swallowed by a great fish, whose mission to Nineveh reveals God''s compassion even toward Israel''s enemies.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_MICAH','PER_ISR_IRON_AGE','An 8th-century BCE contemporary of Isaiah who called Israel to do justice, love mercy, and walk humbly with God.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_NAHUM','PER_ISR_IRON_AGE','A 7th-century BCE prophet who proclaimed the impending fall of Nineveh as God''s judgment on a cruel empire.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_HABAKKUK','PER_ISR_IRON_AGE','A late 7th-century BCE prophet who questioned God about the Babylonian threat and concluded that the righteous shall live by their faith.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_ZEPHANIAH','PER_ISR_IRON_AGE','A 7th-century BCE Judahite prophet during Josiah''s reign who warned of a sweeping Day of the Lord and promised salvation for a humble remnant.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_HAGGAI','PER_ISR_EXILIC','A post-exilic prophet of 520 BCE who urged the returned exiles to rebuild the Jerusalem temple and promised future glory.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_ZECHARIAH','PER_ISR_EXILIC','A post-exilic prophet, contemporary of Haggai, whose night visions encouraged the temple''s rebuilding and foretold a coming messianic king.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_MALACHI','PER_ISR_EXILIC','The last of the Twelve, a 5th-century BCE prophet who rebuked unfaithfulness and announced a coming messenger before the Day of the Lord.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_ELISHA','PER_ISR_IRON_AGE','A 9th-century BCE prophet of the northern kingdom who succeeded Elijah, receiving a double portion of his spirit and performing many miracles.'),
 ('ENT_ISR_NATHAN','PER_ISR_IRON_AGE','A 10th-century BCE court prophet under King David who delivered the Davidic covenant promise and rebuked David over Bathsheba and Uriah.'),
 ('ENT_NT_TWELVE_APOSTLES','PER_APOSTOLIC','The twelve disciples chosen by Jesus as his closest followers and witnesses, the foundation of the apostolic Church.'),
 ('ENT_NT_FOUR_EVANGELISTS','PER_APOSTOLIC','Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John — the traditional authors of the four canonical Gospels.'),
 ('ENT_NT_PAULINE_CIRCLE','PER_APOSTOLIC','The missionary companions and coworkers of the apostle Paul named in Acts and the epistles — Barnabas, Mark, Luke, Timothy, and Titus.'),
 ('ENT_NT_ANDREW','PER_APOSTOLIC','A fisherman of Bethsaida and brother of Simon Peter, called by Jesus to be a fisher of men and numbered among the Twelve.'),
 ('ENT_NT_JOHN_APOSTLE','PER_APOSTOLIC','Son of Zebedee and brother of James the Greater, traditionally identified with the Beloved Disciple and reckoned both apostle and evangelist.'),
 ('ENT_NT_PHILIP','PER_APOSTOLIC','A native of Bethsaida who, on being called by Jesus, sought out Nathanael with the words ''Come and see.'''),
 ('ENT_NT_BARTHOLOMEW','PER_APOSTOLIC','Listed among the Twelve as Bartholomew and commonly identified with the Nathanael whom Jesus praised as guileless in John''s Gospel.'),
 ('ENT_NT_THOMAS','PER_APOSTOLIC','An apostle called Didymus who doubted the resurrection until he saw the risen Christ, then confessed him as ''My Lord and my God.'''),
 ('ENT_NT_MATTHEW','PER_APOSTOLIC','A tax collector (the Levi of Mark and Luke) called by Jesus, numbered among the Twelve and traditionally credited with the First Gospel.'),
 ('ENT_NT_JAMES_ALPHAEUS','PER_APOSTOLIC','An apostle named in all four lists of the Twelve as the son of Alphaeus, distinct from James the son of Zebedee.'),
 ('ENT_NT_JUDE_THADDAEUS','PER_APOSTOLIC','An apostle listed as Thaddaeus in Matthew and Mark and as Judas son (or brother) of James in Luke and Acts.'),
 ('ENT_NT_SIMON_ZEALOT','PER_APOSTOLIC','An apostle of the Twelve called the Zealot (or Cananaean) to distinguish him from Simon Peter.'),
 ('ENT_NT_JUDAS_ISCARIOT','PER_APOSTOLIC','The apostle who betrayed Jesus for thirty pieces of silver and afterward died, his place among the Twelve filled by Matthias.'),
 ('ENT_NT_MATTHIAS','PER_APOSTOLIC','A disciple who had followed Jesus from his baptism and was chosen by lot to take the place of Judas Iscariot among the Twelve.'),
 ('ENT_NT_MARK','PER_APOSTOLIC','John Mark, a companion of Paul, Barnabas, and Peter, traditionally identified as the author of the Second Gospel.'),
 ('ENT_NT_LUKE','PER_APOSTOLIC','A physician and companion of Paul, traditionally credited with the Third Gospel and the Acts of the Apostles.'),
 ('ENT_NT_BARNABAS','PER_APOSTOLIC','A Levite of Cyprus surnamed Barnabas (''son of encouragement'') who introduced Paul to the apostles and traveled with him as a missionary.'),
 ('ENT_NT_TIMOTHY','PER_APOSTOLIC','A disciple of Lystra, son of a Jewish mother and Greek father, who became Paul''s close coworker and the recipient of two epistles.'),
 ('ENT_NT_TITUS','PER_APOSTOLIC','A Greek coworker of Paul, sent to Corinth and left in Crete to set its churches in order, and the recipient of the Epistle to Titus.'),
 ('ENT_NT_LAZARUS_BETHANY','PER_APOSTOLIC','The brother of Martha and Mary of Bethany, whom Jesus raised from the dead after four days in the tomb.'),
 ('ENT_NT_MARTHA','PER_APOSTOLIC','A sister of Lazarus and Mary who served Jesus at Bethany and confessed him as the Christ, the Son of God.'),
 ('ENT_NT_NICODEMUS','PER_APOSTOLIC','A Pharisee and member of the Sanhedrin who came to Jesus by night and later helped Joseph of Arimathea bury him.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_PROPHETS','PER_ISL_EARLY','The collective of prophets named in the Qur''an, from Adam to Muhammad, sent to guide humanity to the worship of the one God.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_ULU_AL_AZM','PER_ISL_EARLY','Ulu al-Azm (''those of firm resolve'') are the five greatest messengers in Islam: Nuh, Ibrahim, Musa, Isa, and Muhammad.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_ADAM','PER_ISL_EARLY','Adam, the first man and first prophet in Islam, created by God and taught the names of all things; the Islamic reception of the Biblical Adam.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_NUH','PER_ISL_EARLY','Nuh built the Ark at God''s command and was saved with the believers from the Flood; the Islamic reception of Noah.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_HUD','PER_ISL_EARLY','Hud was sent to the ancient Arabian people of ''Ad to call them from idolatry; an Arabian prophet with no Biblical counterpart.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_SALIH','PER_ISL_EARLY','Salih was sent to the Arabian people of Thamud with the sign of the she-camel; an Arabian prophet with no Biblical counterpart.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_IBRAHIM','PER_ISL_EARLY','Ibrahim, the friend of God, patriarch of monotheism who with his son built the Kaaba; the Islamic reception of Abraham.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_LUT','PER_ISL_EARLY','Lut warned his people against immorality before their destruction; the Islamic reception of Lot.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_ISMAIL','PER_ISL_EARLY','Ismail, son of Ibrahim, helped build the Kaaba and is regarded in Islam as the son offered in sacrifice; the Islamic reception of Ishmael.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_ISHAQ','PER_ISL_EARLY','Ishaq, son of Ibrahim, was given to him in old age and continued the prophetic line; the Islamic reception of Isaac.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_YAQUB','PER_ISL_EARLY','Yaqub (Israil), son of Ishaq and father of Yusuf, was a prophet and patriarch; the Islamic reception of Jacob.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_YUSUF','PER_ISL_EARLY','Yusuf, son of Yaqub, was sold into Egypt and rose to power, subject of the Qur''an''s ''most beautiful story''; the Islamic reception of Joseph.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_AYYUB','PER_ISL_EARLY','Ayyub endured severe affliction with patience and was restored by God, an exemplar of sabr; the Islamic reception of Job.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_SHUAYB','PER_ISL_EARLY','Shu''ayb was sent to the people of Madyan to enjoin honest dealing and monotheism; an Arabian prophet often linked, but not equated, with Jethro.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_MUSA','PER_ISL_EARLY','Musa, the one to whom God spoke directly, led the Israelites from Egypt and received the Tawrah; the Islamic reception of Moses.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_HARUN','PER_ISL_EARLY','Harun was the brother of Musa and his appointed helper and spokesman; the Islamic reception of Aaron.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_DHUL_KIFL','PER_ISL_EARLY','Dhul-Kifl is a patient prophet named among the righteous, commonly identified by Muslim tradition with Ezekiel.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_DAWUD','PER_ISL_EARLY','Dawud, the prophet-king who slew Jalut and received the Zabur, was given a beautiful voice and wisdom in judgment; the Islamic reception of David.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_SULAYMAN','PER_ISL_EARLY','Sulayman, son of Dawud, was a prophet-king granted command over wind and jinn and knowledge of the speech of animals; the Islamic reception of Solomon.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_ILYAS','PER_ISL_EARLY','Ilyas called his people away from the worship of Baal to the one God; the Islamic reception of Elijah.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_AL_YASA','PER_ISL_EARLY','Al-Yasa is named among the excellent prophets and follows in the line of Ilyas; the Islamic reception of Elisha.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_YUNUS','PER_ISL_EARLY','Yunus, also called Dhul-Nun, was swallowed by a great fish and delivered after repenting, then sent to a people who believed; the Islamic reception of Jonah.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_ZAKARIYA','PER_ISL_EARLY','Zakariya was guardian of Maryam and was granted the son Yahya in old age; counterpart of the New Testament Zechariah, father of John the Baptist.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_YAHYA','PER_ISL_EARLY','Yahya, son of Zakariya, was given wisdom as a child and was pure and devout; the Islamic reception of John the Baptist.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_ISA','PER_ISL_EARLY','Isa al-Masih, son of Maryam, was born of a virgin, given the Injil, and worked miracles by God''s leave, regarded in Islam as prophet and not divine; the Islamic reception of Jesus.'),
 ('ENT_ISL_LUQMAN','PER_ISL_EARLY','Luqman is a wise man granted hikma by God who gives moral counsel to his son; revered as a sage (and by some a prophet), with no Biblical counterpart.');
